    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #345\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed branch `bb/relay-139-auth-v1-01-08-create-the-authenticatio-thr_ygancw5etr` to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #139: creates the auth-v1 database schema and token primitives.\n\n- **Migration** `0016_auth_schema.sql`: extends `users` with `email` (unique), `password_hash`, and `locale` (default `cs`); adds `sessions` (multi-session per user, unique `token_hash`, `platform` restricted to `web`/`ios`/`macos`, expiry/revocation lookup index) and `login_attempts` (email+IP+recency index for throttling).\n- **Primitives** in `backend/packages/data/src/auth/`: Argon2id password hashing (`@node-rs/argon2`), opaque session-token generation/hashing (SHA-256), and constant-time comparison — no JWTs.\n- **Repositories**: `usersStore`, `sessionsStore`, `loginAttemptsStore`, all exported from the package index.\n- **Tests**: unit tests for the crypto primitives and an integration suite covering duplicate email/token rejection, multiple live sessions per user, active-session filtering (expired/revoked), and login-attempt throttling counts.\n\nVerified: full `pnpm run test` (unit, integration, e2e), workspace-wide `tsc -b`, and `check:boundaries` all clean, aside from one pre-existing, unrelated, timing-sensitive flaky test in `propertyTypeMigration.test.ts`.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
