    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #345\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nNo remaining changes to commit — everything from this turn's work (the `develop` merge and the follow-up test fixes) was already committed and pushed in the previous step. Verified the branch is up to date on origin.\n\nBranch: `bb/relay-139-auth-v1-01-08-create-the-authenticatio-thr_ygancw5etr`\n\nThis branch implements issue #139 (auth-v1 01/08): extends `users` with `email`/`password_hash`/`locale`, adds `sessions` and `login_attempts` tables, and adds token primitives (Argon2id password hashing via `@node-rs/argon2`, opaque session tokens hashed with SHA-256 for storage, constant-time comparison). It has since been merged with `develop` to resolve a conflict (including a migration-ordinal collision, resolved by renumbering to `0025_auth_schema.sql`) and a knock-on test regression in unrelated approval-request tests that inserted bare `users` rows. Full test suite (unit/integration/e2e), migration numbering check, dependency-boundary check, and typecheck all pass cleanly.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
